The second beta of iOS 27.3 includes a new "Ask About Page" feature for <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/Siri-AI.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="895" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1051103" /><br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can see the entire content of a webpage, including content that isn't currently in view on the screen. If you're looking at a website with a long menu, for example, you can ask &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; to surface all of the options that are gluten-free. Or if you're getting ready for a trip, you can ask &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; to read through a long guide and put together a packing list based on what's on the page. <br/>
<br/>
Right now, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; has on-screen intelligence, but it relies on what's in view. Access to a full webpage will make &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; more useful for summarizing content. <br/>
<br/>
In the first beta of iOS 27.3, Apple expanded what &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can do in and across apps like Calendar, Files, Finder, Journal, Mail, Maps, Messages, Music, Notes, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a>, Preview, Reminders, Safari, Shortcuts, and Weather.<br/>
<br/>
In Mail, for example, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can unsubscribe you from mailing lists and undo recently sent messages. In Weather, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can add locations to your weather list, or control weather notifications. In Safari, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can clear browsing history, manage tabs and windows, save articles to a Reading List, and close duplicate tabs. In Files, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can organize content, delete files you haven't accessed for a set period of time, and more.<br/>
<br/>
